record akr.papercut.collated-1-papercuts-from-evidence-intake/1 : papercut {
    title "Collated 1 papercut from Evidence-intake-project"
    state verified
    statement """
        Collated 1 papercut from /mnt/Samsung980_1TB/Rust-projects on 2026-08-09 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.ran-knowledge-context-goal-on-a-project-whose [about akr]
        Ran knowledge.context --goal on a project whose ledger held only the namespace stub in project.akr; it failed with AKR-X001 "does not resolve to a record" rather than saying the ledger is empty. On a fresh project that reads as a broken tool call. A distinct message ("no records yet; start with knowledge.propose") would tell an agent to author the first record instead of retrying with different goal strings.
        """
    observed_at git:de899cd260ab7b8f303a53ed5051118f211c2eb9
    about "akr"
    collated [
        "evidence-intake-project.papercut.ran-knowledge-context-goal-on-a-project-whose"
    ]
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record akr.papercut.collated-1-papercuts-from-evidence-intake-2/1 : papercut {
    title "Collated 1 papercut from Evidence-intake-project"
    state verified
    statement """
        Collated 1 papercut from .. on 2026-08-19 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-revise-on-a-proposed-decision-in [about akr]
        knowledge.revise on a proposed decision (in-place, rev stays 1) silently dropped the record's source attributions when `sources` was omitted, and passing `sources` explicitly on a later revise did not write them back (content hash unchanged, no `source` block in the file); knowledge.propose with the same payload had persisted them. Also, propose rejects a source with start_line/end_line alone (needs start_byte/end_byte too) which forces callers to compute byte offsets by hand.
        """
    observed_at git:daad9b2500fec8acbb1b684e03de4a497bc21af4
    about "akr"
    collated [ "evidence-intake-project.papercut.knowledge-revise-on-a-proposed-decision-in" ]
    author "GitHub Uploader"
    created_at 2026-08-19
}

record akr.papercut.collated-10-papercuts-from-evidence-intake/1 : papercut {
    title "Collated 10 papercuts from Evidence-intake-project, Kitchen-Concept, Lege-ecosystem, SaveYourSkin and 5 more"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Collated 10 papercuts from /mnt/Samsung980_1TB/Rust-projects on 2026-08-09 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.a-release-profiler-rebuild-from-the-repository
        A release-profiler rebuild from the repository root rejected `--features bench-profiling` because the `pdfium-diff` tool is deliberately outside the workspace; the feature belongs to its own manifest. The command must run from `lege-pdf/render/tools/pdfium-diff` or pass that manifest explicitly.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.after-committing-validated-akr-record-changes [about akr]
        After committing validated AKR record changes with ordinary Git, `akr lock --check` rejected the embedded build commit because the lock was generated against the parent source commit. The workflow needs an atomic documented commit path or an explicit follow-up lock-only commit; otherwise a seemingly clean knowledge commit fails the required post-commit audit.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.at-handoff-knowledge-validate-withheld-its [about akr]
        At handoff, knowledge.validate withheld its entire 8.5k-token result and suggested narrower arguments even though the tool exposes no scope/filter argument; diagnosing required the separate `akr check` CLI (the protocol's `knowledge.validate` name is not a CLI subcommand). A summarized diagnostics mode would make the required handoff check actionable.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.correcting-an-inaccurate-papercut-via-knowledge [about akr]
        Correcting an inaccurate papercut via knowledge.supersede failed because the connected workspace vocabulary 0.1 does not support the tool schema's `new_key` option. The correction had to reuse the original key instead of creating a clearer replacement key.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.creating-the-finalization-work-record-failed [about akr]
        Creating the finalization work record failed because `depends_on` cannot reference a completed work record, but the propose schema does not identify which relation should capture historical provenance. The write was retried with only the live decision dependency.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.knowledge-context-withheld-a-4-1k-token-bundle [about akr]
        knowledge.context withheld a 4.1k-token bundle even though I requested a 16k budget, then advised requesting fewer tokens. The MCP response ceiling is lower than the tool's advertised budget parameter, so context had to be retried with narrower paths.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.running-cargo-fmt-check-from-lege-pdf-render
        Running `cargo fmt --check` from `lege-pdf/render` failed with “Failed to find targets” because that directory is not a usable Cargo formatting root even though renderer crates are nested beneath it. The verification workflow needs to point rustfmt/cargo at the concrete crate or the external tool manifest.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.the-targeted-renderer-image-clippy-check-is
        The targeted renderer/image clippy check is blocked by an unrelated existing `-D clippy::expect-used` violation in `lege-pdf/render/crates/pdf-document/src/pages.rs:594`, reached through `pdf-cli` dependencies. Renderer/image tests pass, but the documented clippy gate cannot complete until that pre-existing lint is resolved or the check is scoped differently.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.while-recording-the-renderer-decision-knowledge [about akr]
        While recording the renderer decision, knowledge.propose rejected a dotted decision topic even though the key is dot-delimited; the topic segment syntax was not apparent from the tool schema, so the write had to be retried with a single hyphenated segment. The response also warned that the connected MCP vocabulary 0.2 is newer than the workspace build vocabulary 0.1.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.while-reproducing-the-structures-pdf-mrc
        While reproducing the Structures.pdf MRC profile, the performance handoff labels the 2222x3191 run as scale 2.0833333, but the supplied 444.4x638.2-point page produces 926x1330 at that scale and 2222x3191 at scale 5.0. Benchmark records should store both requested scale and resulting dimensions so comparisons cannot silently mix them.
        """
    observed_at git:de899cd260ab7b8f303a53ed5051118f211c2eb9
    collated [
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.a-release-profiler-rebuild-from-the-repository",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.after-committing-validated-akr-record-changes",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.at-handoff-knowledge-validate-withheld-its",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.correcting-an-inaccurate-papercut-via-knowledge",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.creating-the-finalization-work-record-failed",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.knowledge-context-withheld-a-4-1k-token-bundle",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.running-cargo-fmt-check-from-lege-pdf-render",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.the-targeted-renderer-image-clippy-check-is",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.while-recording-the-renderer-decision-knowledge",
