    ]
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record akr.papercut.collated-10-papercuts-from-evidence-intake/2 : papercut {
    title "Collated 6 AKR papercuts from Lege-ecosystem"
    state verified
    statement """
        Collated 6 AKR papercuts from /mnt/Samsung980_1TB/Rust-projects on 2026-08-09 (D-030). Four untagged Lege-ecosystem papercuts were mistakenly absorbed by the previous revision and are excluded here; each retained source key is in the collated slot.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.after-committing-validated-akr-record-changes [about akr]
        After committing validated AKR record changes with ordinary Git, `akr lock --check` rejected the embedded build commit because the lock was generated against the parent source commit. The workflow needs an atomic documented commit path or an explicit follow-up lock-only commit; otherwise a seemingly clean knowledge commit fails the required post-commit audit.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.at-handoff-knowledge-validate-withheld-its [about akr]
        At handoff, knowledge.validate withheld its entire 8.5k-token result and suggested narrower arguments even though the tool exposes no scope/filter argument; diagnosing required the separate `akr check` CLI (the protocol's `knowledge.validate` name is not a CLI subcommand). A summarized diagnostics mode would make the required handoff check actionable.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.correcting-an-inaccurate-papercut-via-knowledge [about akr]
        Correcting an inaccurate papercut via knowledge.supersede failed because the connected workspace vocabulary 0.1 does not support the tool schema's `new_key` option. The correction had to reuse the original key instead of creating a clearer replacement key.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.creating-the-finalization-work-record-failed [about akr]
        Creating the finalization work record failed because `depends_on` cannot reference a completed work record, but the propose schema does not identify which relation should capture historical provenance. The write was retried with only the live decision dependency.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.knowledge-context-withheld-a-4-1k-token-bundle [about akr]
        knowledge.context withheld a 4.1k-token bundle even though I requested a 16k budget, then advised requesting fewer tokens. The MCP response ceiling is lower than the tool's advertised budget parameter, so context had to be retried with narrower paths.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.while-recording-the-renderer-decision-knowledge [about akr]
        While recording the renderer decision, knowledge.propose rejected a dotted decision topic even though the key is dot-delimited; the topic segment syntax was not apparent from the tool schema, so the write had to be retried with a single hyphenated segment. The response also warned that the connected MCP vocabulary 0.2 is newer than the workspace build vocabulary 0.1.
        """
    observed_at git:de899cd260ab7b8f303a53ed5051118f211c2eb9
    about "akr"
    collated [
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.after-committing-validated-akr-record-changes",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.at-handoff-knowledge-validate-withheld-its",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.correcting-an-inaccurate-papercut-via-knowledge",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.creating-the-finalization-work-record-failed",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.knowledge-context-withheld-a-4-1k-token-bundle",
        "lege-ecosystem-perf.papercut.while-recording-the-renderer-decision-knowledge"
    ]
    supersedes [ @akr.papercut.collated-10-papercuts-from-evidence-intake/1 ]
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record akr.papercut.collated-10-papercuts-from-evidence-intake-2/1 : papercut {
    title "Collated 10 papercuts from Evidence-intake-project, Kitchen-Concept, Lege-ecosystem, SaveYourSkin and 1 more"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Collated 10 papercuts from /mnt/Samsung980_1TB/Rust-projects on 2026-08-23 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.proposing-records-with-line-based-citations [about akr]
        Proposing records with line-based citations into a registered source: every citation whose end_line fell on a blank line was accepted by knowledge.propose but then failed validation with AKR-S022 (byte range covers one line fewer). Eight revises to fix. Propose should either reject or normalise the range at write time.

        ## Evidence-intake-project @evidence-intake-project.papercut.while-proposing-a-decision-through-knowledge [about akr]
        While proposing a decision through knowledge.propose I used the common `statement` slot; decisions instead require a `decision` slot, which is easy to miss without calling knowledge.explain first.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.knowledge-propose-documents-scope-as-array [about akr]
        knowledge.propose documents scope as Array<unknown> but does not describe accepted scope forms; a natural {path: ...} object failed with AKR-C004 and required a schema lookup/retry.

        ## Kitchen-Concept @kitchen.papercut.knowledge-propose-exposes-scope-only-as-array [about akr]
        knowledge.propose exposes `scope` only as Array<unknown>; passing documented-looking `{path: ...}` objects failed with AKR-C004 and did not identify the accepted MCP representation. The schema should enumerate valid scope forms.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.creating-the-publication-work-record-first [about akr]
        Creating the publication work record first failed because work requires an intent slot and rejects topic; the schema requirements were only disclosed after the write attempt.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.finishing-the-stair-descent-task-the-global [about akr]
        Finishing the stair-descent task, the global instructions ask for `akr scratch prune` / `akr scratch list`, but the installed akr CLI (~/.local/bin/akr) rejects `scratch` as an unknown command, so scratch hygiene had to be done by hand (the session's own outputs were kept under .agent/scratch/stair-tread-descent/). Either the CLI is behind the instructions or the command has another name.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-search-and-knowledge-start-return [about akr]
        knowledge.search and knowledge.start return zero results for any multi-word query (e.g. "profession resident courtier", "NPC AI agency intent") on this ledger while single words ("profession", "mind", "verb") return many; the FTS index appears to AND all terms, so natural-language task queries silently miss. Orientation worked only after splitting into single-word searches.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.after-akr-scratch-keep-quality-rate-curve [about akr]
        After `akr scratch keep quality-rate-curve-closure-20260823` and `akr build`, `akr scratch list` showed the entry as kept, but knowledge.evidence_add twice rejected a file inside it with AKR-C004 as disposable. MCP scratch-keep detection appears out of sync with the CLI metadata.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-exposes-scope-as-array [about akr]
        knowledge.propose exposes scope as Array<unknown>; passing intuitive {path: ...} objects fails only with 'unknown scope form'. The accepted MCP shape is {form: 'path', glob: ...}, which should be expressed in the tool schema or error.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-exposes-topic-for-every [about akr]
        knowledge.propose exposes `topic` for every record kind, but a work proposal containing it fails only after full validation with AKR-T034 because topic is normative-only. The tool schema or preflight should state/reject this earlier.
        """
    observed_at git:1414d0107e6bde1dfb7b05911e0be53a15b1b33d
    about "akr"
    collated [
        "evidence-intake-project.papercut.proposing-records-with-line-based-citations",
        "evidence-intake-project.papercut.while-proposing-a-decision-through-knowledge",
        "kitchen.papercut.knowledge-propose-documents-scope-as-array",
        "kitchen.papercut.knowledge-propose-exposes-scope-only-as-array",
        "lege-ecosystem.papercut.creating-the-publication-work-record-first",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.finishing-the-stair-descent-task-the-global",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-search-and-knowledge-start-return",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.after-akr-scratch-keep-quality-rate-curve",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-exposes-scope-as-array",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-propose-exposes-topic-for-every"
    ]
    created_at 2026-08-23
}

