record akr.papercut.collated-8-papercuts-from-lege-ecosystem/1 : papercut {
    title "Collated 8 papercuts from Lege-ecosystem and SaveYourSkin"
    state verified
    statement """
        Collated 8 papercuts from /mnt/Samsung980_1TB/Rust-projects on 2026-08-13 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-proposing-the-jbig2-smask-preservation [about akr]
        While proposing the JBIG2 SMask preservation work record, source citations with start_line/end_line were rejected because AKR also requires exact start_byte/end_byte. The proposal schema does not make that coupled range requirement obvious at authoring time; I retried with path-level citations.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.after-completing-all-g1-g7-children-revising [about akr]
        After completing all G1-G7 children, revising the spatial track from active to completed was refused because active normative records legitimately depend on the track and the validator treated the resulting completed revision as a superseded target (`slot depends_on may not reference ... /2, which is superseded`). A completed planning prerequisite should remain satisfiable, or the diagnostic should identify the exact dependent that requires repointing.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.completing-sound-acoustic-studio-and-walk-test [about akr]
        Completing sound-acoustic-studio-and-walk-test was refused because its inherited part_of relation still targets superseded sound-design/1 even though context also derives it under /2. The child must be revised to the current parent before completion; superseding a track should ideally retarget or clearly disposition child parentage.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.completing-sound-source-profile-and-lod-audit [about akr]
        Completing sound-source-profile-and-lod-audit failed because its recovered part_of relations still included terminal sound-design/1 alongside the current track, even though the context bundle had already dispositioned it into sound-design/2. Completion required a relation-only revision first.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-revise-activates-a-proposed [about akr]
        knowledge.revise activates a proposed constraint cleanly, but a follow-up revision using `retired_claims` (with or without replacement claims) emits malformed-source parser diagnostics such as unclosed brackets and `constraint has no slot claim`. The API appears to serialize claim retirement incorrectly, preventing removal of a now-false live-counterexample claim.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-search-could-not-refresh-or-use-the [about akr]
        knowledge.search could not refresh or use the ledger index because the cache was built without FTS5, forcing direct reads of already-known record keys for gameplay prioritization.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-proposing-a-work-record-i-used-a-natural [about akr]
        While proposing a work record I used a natural `summary` slot and had to retry after schema rejection; surfacing the valid kind-specific slots in the proposal tool description or accepting `summary` as an alias would avoid this round trip.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-recording-an-unplanned-completed [about akr]
        While recording an unplanned completed integration slice, knowledge.propose did not surface the required `work.intent` slot until validation rejected the first write; including kind-specific required slots in the tool schema or error-free template would avoid the retry.
        """
    observed_at git:94498f67d73d18323a5b06a3e5e59e307286947b
    about "akr"
    collated [
        "lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-proposing-the-jbig2-smask-preservation",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.after-completing-all-g1-g7-children-revising",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.completing-sound-acoustic-studio-and-walk-test",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.completing-sound-source-profile-and-lod-audit",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-revise-activates-a-proposed",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-search-could-not-refresh-or-use-the",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.while-proposing-a-work-record-i-used-a-natural",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.while-recording-an-unplanned-completed"
    ]
    created_at 2026-08-13
}

record akr.papercut.collated-8-papercuts-from-lege-ecosystem-legeos/1 : papercut {
    title "Collated 8 papercuts from Lege-ecosystem, LegeOS, jpegXL-rs and orderflower"
    state verified
    statement """
        Collated 8 papercuts from \\?\D:\Rust-projects on 2026-08-18 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.knowledge-start-returned-a-truncated-preview [about akr]
        knowledge.start returned a truncated preview and required an immediate second call with its suggested lower budget, even though the task/path query had no planning matches; the papercut logger then also required a namespace retry in this multi-namespace workspace. Returning the compact no-match session directly and surfacing the namespace requirement earlier would avoid redundant round trips.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-orienting-an-installer-readiness-review [about akr]
        While orienting an installer-readiness review, knowledge.context rejected an absolute Windows path using native backslashes; its path-glob interface requires forward slashes even on Windows. The diagnostic was clear, but accepting native separators would make Windows usage smoother.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-proposing-installer-work-knowledge [about akr]
        While proposing installer work, knowledge.propose accepted free-form acceptance.method strings in its tool schema but the ledger requires the enum command/manual/observation, producing low-level parser errors before the clearer T012 diagnostic. The tool description or JSON schema should expose the enum.

        ## LegeOS @legeos.papercut.promoting-decisions-to-active-with-akr-revise [about akr]
        Promoting decisions to active with `akr revise <key> --state active` in text mode printed only "nothing written" — the actual reason (V-021: active decision cites nothing; and V-005: supported_by may not target a constraint, use implements) only appeared with --format json. Text mode should print the blocking diagnostics too.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.the-first-phase-25-work-proposal-was-rejected [about akr]
        The first Phase 25 work proposal was rejected because the work intent was supplied at the top level with an invalid topic slot; retrying with the documented slots.intent form succeeded.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.the-installed-akr-0-3-1-rejected-four-existing [about akr]
        The installed akr 0.3.1 rejected four existing observation records because it expected method instrumented, while current official AKR source accepts the documented method observation. A temporary build from official HEAD was required to read context, update evidence, and validate the ledger.

        ## orderflower @orderflower.papercut.akr-mcp-server-failed-to-connect-at-session [about akr]
        AKR MCP server failed to connect at session start, so knowledge.start/context were unavailable and I had to fall back to the akr CLI. Same pattern as a down integration rather than a workspace problem.

        ## orderflower @orderflower.papercut.knowledge-mcp-server-failed-to-connect-timed [about akr]
        knowledge.* MCP server failed to connect (timed out). Used the akr CLI instead; start/context still work, but the protocol's first-call path is the MCP tools.
        """
    observed_at git:9b534026ceff084e33ac987b959f3824eabaa409
    about "akr"
    collated [
        "lege-ecosystem.papercut.knowledge-start-returned-a-truncated-preview",
        "lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-orienting-an-installer-readiness-review",
        "lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-proposing-installer-work-knowledge",
        "legeos.papercut.promoting-decisions-to-active-with-akr-revise",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.the-first-phase-25-work-proposal-was-rejected",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.the-installed-akr-0-3-1-rejected-four-existing",
        "orderflower.papercut.akr-mcp-server-failed-to-connect-at-session",
        "orderflower.papercut.knowledge-mcp-server-failed-to-connect-timed"
    ]
    author "GitHub Uploader"
    created_at 2026-08-18
}

record akr.papercut.collated-9-papercuts-from-lege-ecosystem/1 : papercut {
    title "Collated 9 papercuts from Lege-ecosystem, SaveYourSkin and jpegXL-rs"
    state verified
    statement """
        Collated 9 papercuts from /mnt/Samsung980_1TB/Rust-projects on 2026-08-12 (D-030). Each source key is also in the collated slot, which is the dedup set for the next run; the sisters were read and never written.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.knowledge-get-did-not-display-a-work-record-s [about akr]
        knowledge.get did not display a work record's acceptance checks even at canonical detail, so knowledge.complete had to fail once to reveal the four check IDs needed for evidence mapping.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-creating-ocr-work-records-from-a [about akr]
        While creating OCR work records from a registered source, using the apparent @source.<id> derived_from form produced AKR-L001. The tool could make the source-vs-record citation distinction clearer in relation errors; papercut logging also required a namespace only after the first call failed.

        ## Lege-ecosystem @lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-creating-the-auto-toc-work-record [about akr]
        While creating the auto-TOC work record, `knowledge.propose` accepted a `topic` argument in its API schema but rejected it at validation because planning kinds cannot use topics. The schema could make that kind-specific restriction visible before submission.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-start-foregrounded-the-blender [about akr]
        knowledge.start foregrounded the Blender authority decision, but knowledge.context rejects decisions as goals; the handoff could expose the nearest live milestone/track alongside the decision to avoid a failed orientation call.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.on-akr-0-3-0-for-windows-knowledge-start [about akr]
        On AKR 0.3.0 for Windows, knowledge.start ignored budget_tokens 1400, assembled about 2116 tokens, then withheld the entire handoff at the 2000-token cap. A later knowledge.context request at 1850 returned a bundle labeled about 4345 tokens, so budget and hard-limit behavior were inconsistent and required multiple slow retries.

        ## SaveYourSkin @saveyourskin.papercut.while-importing-a-connected-sound-design-record [about akr]
        While importing a connected sound-design record batch, knowledge.propose reported nested validation failures only after each write attempt; a dry-run/schema-introspection mode for slots and reference heads would prevent cascaded retries. One policy also accepts `rationale`, not the otherwise common `context` slot.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-start-withheld-a-6440-token [about akr]
        knowledge.start withheld a ~6440-token orientation bundle despite a requested 18000-token budget because of an internal 2000-token hard limit; discovering the governing goal therefore requires a separate search/context round trip.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.orienting-on-this-project-through-the-knowledge [about akr]
        Orienting on this project through the knowledge.* MCP tools failed at the first step: knowledge.start truncated at a 2000-token hard limit even with budget_tokens=1800 (estimated 3245, continuation null, no way to page), and knowledge.search truncated at 1000 tokens with 20 results. Both returned only a truncation notice with zero usable content, so the sanctioned fallback (AGENTS.md section 10) of reading .akr/records/**/*.akr and docs/generated/ directly was the only route to a project summary. A continuation token, or honouring budget_tokens above the hard limit, would make the tools usable on a ledger this size.

        ## jpegXL-rs @jpegxl-rs.papercut.while-repairing-phase-4l-evidence-chronology [about akr]
        While repairing Phase 4L evidence chronology, knowledge.revise returned the completed work revision to proposed even though the call explicitly passed state="completed". A follow-up knowledge.complete restored the intended terminal state; the tool documentation and project gotcha both say re-passing state should preserve it.
        """
    observed_at git:2dd07efa746065e627b1445587e3bb0ca0af553b
    about "akr"
    collated [
        "lege-ecosystem.papercut.knowledge-get-did-not-display-a-work-record-s",
        "lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-creating-ocr-work-records-from-a",
        "lege-ecosystem.papercut.while-creating-the-auto-toc-work-record",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.knowledge-start-foregrounded-the-blender",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.on-akr-0-3-0-for-windows-knowledge-start",
        "saveyourskin.papercut.while-importing-a-connected-sound-design-record",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.knowledge-start-withheld-a-6440-token",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.orienting-on-this-project-through-the-knowledge",
        "jpegxl-rs.papercut.while-repairing-phase-4l-evidence-chronology"
    ]
    created_at 2026-08-12
}

record akr.papercut.completing-a-milestone-failed-because-a/1 : papercut {
    title "Completing a milestone failed because a downstream depends_on edge…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Completing a milestone failed because a downstream depends_on edge treated completed work like abandonment, forcing agents to remove the satisfied dependency and manufacture lifecycle revisions. Completion should satisfy depends_on while preserving the edge as provenance.
        """
    observed_at git:de899cd260ab7b8f303a53ed5051118f211c2eb9
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record akr.papercut.completing-a-milestone-failed-because-a/2 : papercut {
    title "Completing a milestone failed because a downstream depends_on edge…"
    state withdrawn
    statement """
        Completing a milestone failed because a downstream depends_on edge treated completed work like abandonment, forcing agents to remove the satisfied dependency and manufacture lifecycle revisions. Completion should satisfy depends_on while preserving the edge as provenance.

        RESOLVED: a completed `depends_on` target is now exempt from the terminal-reference
        rule, so completion satisfies a prerequisite and the edge survives as provenance.
        Abandonment and supersession still invalidate it. crates/akr-core/src/validate/rules.rs;
        docs/05-validation-rules.md §AKR-L021.
        """
    observed_at git:de899cd260ab7b8f303a53ed5051118f211c2eb9
    supersedes [ @akr.papercut.completing-a-milestone-failed-because-a/1 ]
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-09
}

record akr.papercut.crates-akr-cli-tests-commands-rs-is-the-only/1 : papercut {
    title "crates/akr-cli/tests/commands.rs is the only file in the repo committed…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        crates/akr-cli/tests/commands.rs is the only file in the repo committed with CRLF endings (git ls-files --eol: 1 of N) and there is no .gitattributes. Running the documented `cargo fmt` rewrites it LF-only, so git reports every one of its ~400 lines as delete+re-add — a ~900-line phantom diff around a small change. `cargo fmt --check` does NOT flag it, so the verify-distribution.sh fmt gate stays green and nothing warns you. This cost two agents real review time on one papercut fix, both of whom had to diagnose it independently. Either commit that file as LF like every other file, or add a .gitattributes that pins the convention.
        """
    observed_at git:9b534026ceff084e33ac987b959f3824eabaa409
    author "claude-opus-5"
    created_at 2026-08-18
}

record akr.papercut.crates-akr-cli-tests-commands-rs-is-the-only/2 : papercut {
    title "crates/akr-cli/tests/commands.rs is the only file in the repo committed…"
    state withdrawn
    statement """
        crates/akr-cli/tests/commands.rs is the only file in the repo committed with CRLF endings (git ls-files --eol: 1 of N) and there is no .gitattributes. Running the documented `cargo fmt` rewrites it LF-only, so git reports every one of its ~400 lines as delete+re-add — a ~900-line phantom diff around a small change. `cargo fmt --check` does NOT flag it, so the verify-distribution.sh fmt gate stays green and nothing warns you. This cost two agents real review time on one papercut fix, both of whom had to diagnose it independently. Either commit that file as LF like every other file, or add a .gitattributes that pins the convention.

        RESOLVED in af11eae. .gitattributes pins `* text=auto eol=lf` for the whole tree and the
        file was renormalised in a commit of its own, so the rewrite never has to be read as
        part of a change with content in it.
        """
    observed_at git:9b534026ceff084e33ac987b959f3824eabaa409
    supersedes [ @akr.papercut.crates-akr-cli-tests-commands-rs-is-the-only/1 ]
    author "claude-opus-5"
    created_at 2026-08-18
}

record akr.papercut.every-akr-c0nn-usage-refusal-raised-through/1 : papercut {
    title "Every AKR-C0nn usage refusal raised through EnvError exits 3…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Every AKR-C0nn usage refusal raised through EnvError exits 3 (environment) rather than the exit 2 the diagnostic registry documents for that class — akr evidence add --result nope and --artifact under scratch both do it, so a caller branching on exit status reads a usage error as a broken checkout. The mapping lives in session::EnvError and predates the collated batch.
        """
    observed_at git:1414d0107e6bde1dfb7b05911e0be53a15b1b33d
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-22
}

record akr.papercut.evidence-recorded-after-tests-but-before/1 : papercut {
    title "Evidence recorded after tests but before  pointed at the parent commit,…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Evidence recorded after tests but before  pointed at the parent commit, so the newly committed completed work immediately failed AKR-R022 as evidence predating its content. The change protocol needs a supported two-phase completion flow or evidence tied to the prepared implementation tree instead of an unknowable future commit.
        """
    observed_at git:03e4af3c2e62cb07ab00436e512bedc41cd88436
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-11
}

record akr.papercut.evidence-recorded-after-tests-but-before/2 : papercut {
    title "Evidence recorded after tests but before  pointed at the parent commit,…"
    state withdrawn
    statement """
        Evidence recorded after tests but before  pointed at the parent commit, so the newly committed completed work immediately failed AKR-R022 as evidence predating its content. The change protocol needs a supported two-phase completion flow or evidence tied to the prepared implementation tree instead of an unknowable future commit.

        RESOLVED: the change protocol grew the two-phase flow this asked for — `akr change
        prepare --staged` and `akr change verify --staged` bind evidence to the staged tree
        rather than to an unknowable future commit, and AKR-R022's registry entry records that
        evidence co-committed with the content it verifies is current.
        docs/16-change-protocol.md.
        """
    observed_at git:03e4af3c2e62cb07ab00436e512bedc41cd88436
    supersedes [ @akr.papercut.evidence-recorded-after-tests-but-before/1 ]
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-11
}

record akr.papercut.historical-port-design-gap-recovered-from-a/1 : papercut {
    title "Historical-port design gap, recovered from a lost agent session…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Historical-port design gap, recovered from a lost agent session (originally logged in the bpg-rs ledger as bpg.papercut.v-020-s-descendant-commit-freshness-gate-akr/1). A single-commit port of old history validated clean before commit, but once the ledger was committed akr check raised 19 AKR-R022: D-016/V-020's descendant-commit rule wants each completed record's evidence to postdate the record's last content change, which is structurally impossible for a transcription of history whose evidence commits predate the port commit. RESOLVED by D-028 (2026-08-05): a completed record carrying source { kind legacy } waives the descendant-commit comparison only (evidence must still resolve, record result pass, and be a commit the repo has). Ports like bpg-rs and the planned jp2lam go green once re-checked with a D-028 binary and their completed records carry a legacy source block.
        """
    observed_at git:047a684214734d19ebc8a477030ceb9cfbc98ceb
    author "fugu"
    created_at 2026-08-05
}

record akr.papercut.historical-port-design-gap-recovered-from-a/2 : papercut {
    title "Historical-port design gap, recovered from a lost agent session…"
    state withdrawn
    statement """
        Historical-port design gap, recovered from a lost agent session (originally logged in the bpg-rs ledger as bpg.papercut.v-020-s-descendant-commit-freshness-gate-akr/1). A single-commit port of old history validated clean before commit, but once the ledger was committed akr check raised 19 AKR-R022: D-016/V-020's descendant-commit rule wants each completed record's evidence to postdate the record's last content change, which is structurally impossible for a transcription of history whose evidence commits predate the port commit. RESOLVED by D-028 (2026-08-05): a completed record carrying source { kind legacy } waives the descendant-commit comparison only (evidence must still resolve, record result pass, and be a commit the repo has). Ports like bpg-rs and the planned jp2lam go green once re-checked with a D-028 binary and their completed records carry a legacy source block.

        RESOLVED: D-028 (2026-08-05), and the general case by D-029 (2026-08-06). A completed record carrying source { kind legacy } waives the descendant-commit comparison, and the gate now measures definitional change for everyone else.
        """
    observed_at git:047a684214734d19ebc8a477030ceb9cfbc98ceb
    supersedes [ @akr.papercut.historical-port-design-gap-recovered-from-a/1 ]
}

