record akr.papercut.knowledge-context-rejects-completed-work-goals/2 : papercut {
    title "knowledge.context rejects completed work goals with AKR-X002 even when…"
    state withdrawn
    statement """
        knowledge.context rejects completed work goals with AKR-X002 even when the repository protocol says to call context with the exact planning key; corrective follow-up needs a new work record before the prior bundle can be inspected.

        CLOSED as working as designed. A bundle anchors on *intent*, so a terminal goal is
        retrieval-only by design (AKR-X002, docs/09-context-assembly.md §70) and the refusal
        returns a ready-made next command. Corrective follow-up genuinely is new work and wants
        its own record; `akr get` still retrieves the finished one. If the ergonomics still
        bite, that is a design question for a `question` record rather than a defect here.
        """
    observed_at git:911c29573461ba912cc141f49f4d8c05c61ec5e1
    about "akr"
    supersedes [ @akr.papercut.knowledge-context-rejects-completed-work-goals/1 ]
