record akr.papercut.the-cli-help-advertises-edit-for-propose-and/2 : papercut {
    title "The CLI help advertises --edit for propose and revise, but this build…"
    state withdrawn
    statement """
        The CLI help advertises --edit for propose and revise, but this build rejects it as unavailable; the documented path caused an avoidable failed write before falling back to --from.

        RESOLVED in fb3bb92. `--edit` is refused at parse time now, carrying the reason it does
        not exist — an editor is a terminal interaction the MCP surface cannot have, and a flag
        that works from a shell and fails from an agent is worse than one honestly absent. The
        help stopped advertising it earlier; the parser had not.
        """
    observed_at git:de899cd260ab7b8f303a53ed5051118f211c2eb9
