    state withdrawn
    statement """
        While beginning a change transaction, the natural kind 'feature' was rejected because the accepted spelling is the undocumented Conventional Commit abbreviation 'feat'; the error recovers well, but help or aliasing would avoid the retry.

        RESOLVED in fb3bb92. `ChangeKind::from_name` accepts the unabbreviated spellings
        (feature, documentation, performance, bugfix); the stored name stays the Conventional
        Commit abbreviation. The help lists the kinds as well.
        """
    observed_at git:05fea30a52f59775917cf5a1d1ac1241c0392b44
    supersedes [ @akr.papercut.while-beginning-a-change-transaction-the/1 ]
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-11
}

record akr.papercut.while-checking-akr-mcp-without-default-features/1 : papercut {
    title "While checking akr-mcp without default features, the differential…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        While checking akr-mcp without default features, the differential harness first used a stale default-feature target/debug/akr unless that CLI binary was rebuilt explicitly; after rebuilding correctly, two knowledge.start fallback tests still fail because the non-FTS validated-head path omits coverage and workspace_fallback metadata. The budget/pagination tests themselves pass in that configuration.
        """
    observed_at git:2dd07efa746065e627b1445587e3bb0ca0af553b
    about "akr"
    author "codex"
