}

record akr.papercut.while-checking-akr-mcp-without-default-features/2 : papercut {
    title "While checking akr-mcp without default features, the differential…"
    state withdrawn
    statement """
        While checking akr-mcp without default features, the differential harness first used a stale default-feature target/debug/akr unless that CLI binary was rebuilt explicitly; after rebuilding correctly, two knowledge.start fallback tests still fail because the non-FTS validated-head path omits coverage and workspace_fallback metadata. The budget/pagination tests themselves pass in that configuration.

        RESOLVED in fb3bb92, and the report's diagnosis was inverted. `knowledge.start` loses no
        metadata without FTS5 — the non-FTS `start` calls `finish_start` like the other. What
        was real is why nobody could tell: akr-gui took akr-cli with default features while
        every other crate takes its AKR dependencies with `default-features = false`, and
        cargo's feature unification then kept FTS5 on for workspace-level
        `--no-default-features`. Per-package, seven source_library tests failed by asserting
        search hits against a binary that had correctly reported AKR-I022. akr-gui forwards the
        feature now, those tests carry `#[cfg(feature = "fts5")]`, and search_degraded.rs
        asserts the documented degradation. Both configurations pass.
        """
    observed_at git:2dd07efa746065e627b1445587e3bb0ca0af553b
    about "akr"
    supersedes [ @akr.papercut.while-checking-akr-mcp-without-default-features/1 ]
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-08-12
}

